# Keep line endings in the repository LF, whatever the contributor's core.autocrlf says. The
# generated files in cipp/ are written with LF by Node; without this rule a checkout on Windows
# without autocrlf can commit them back with CRLF, and every line then shows up as changed in the
# PR that the workflow opens.
* text=auto

# The templates in CATemplate/ are single-line JSON exported from CIPP, without a trailing
# newline. Leave them byte for byte as CIPP wrote them.
CATemplate/GLOBAL__*.json -text
